title: Revolutionary Government Established
subtitle: We are victorious, but now what?
tags: event

= The German Revolutionary Government

We have successfully overthrown the reactionary government! We must move quickly to transform German society and lay the foundations of a new political system.

[? if Q.kpd_revsupport == 1: The <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span> fought alongside us during the revolutionary struggle, and expect us to cooperate with them as we implement new policies. ?]
[? if Q.kpd_revsupport == 0: The <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span> took up arms during the revolution, but do not trust us. We will have to either convince them to lay down their arms or suppress them by force. ?]
[? if sapd_formed: The <span style="color: #9B0000;">**SAPD**</span> fully support the revolution, and hope we will pursue <span style="color: #9B0000;">**radical**</span> social change. ?]

- @rev_gov: Government Structure
- @rev_elections: Elections
- @rev_opposition: Stance Towards Opposition Parties
- @rev_economy: Economic Policy
- @rev_army: Status of the Reichswehr
- @rev_communists: Dealing with the Communists

@rev_gov
max-visits: 1

With the old political system swept away, we are free to alter Germany's institutions of government as we see fit.

- @anarchy: Abolish the state entirely!
- @councils: Create a federated system of worker councils!
- @centralize: Create a centralized people's republic modelled on the Soviet Union!
- @reform: Reform the existing democratic system to make it more progressive!
- @maintain: Maintain the existing democratic system to ensure stability!

@anarchy
unavailable-subtitle: We are not anarchists.
choose-if: 0;

@councils
subtitle: Supported by: Left, Labor, KPD, [? if sapd_formed: SAPD ?].
on-arrival: Q.council_system = 1; left_dissent += 15; labor_dissent += 10; kpd_relation += 10; workers_spd += 10; workers_kpd += 10; [? if sapd_formed: workers_sapd += 10; ?] reformist_dissent -= 20; z_relation -= 20; dvp_relation -= 20; ddp_relation -= 15;

We have endorsed and recognized the formation of worker councils throughout Germany, and our government has set to work organizing them into a federated governing body. Radical leftists and workers are pleased, while moderates are deeply concerned.

go-to: civil_war_victory.scene.dry
  
@centralize
subtitle: Supported by: KPD.
unavailable-subtitle: There is no support for this outside of the KPD, who do not trust us.
choose-if: Q.kpd_revsupport == 1;
on-arrival: Q.soviet_system = 1; kpd_relation += 30; center_dissent -= 10; labor dissent -= 10; reformist_dissent -= 30; z_relation -= 50; dvp_relation -= 50; ddp_relation -= 50;

We have established a people's republic with a similar structure to that of the Soviet Union, much to the delight of the KPD and the dismay of everyone else, including most of our own party.

go-to: civil_war_victory.scene.dry

@reform:
subtitle: Supported by: Center, Reformists.
on-arrival: Q.reformed_system = 1; center_dissent += 10; reformist_dissent += 30; ddp_relation += 15; z_relation += 5; left_dissent -= 10; kpd_relation -= 10;

We have reformed Germany's parliamentary system to reflect genuine democratic and republican values. The KPD and our party's left-wing are disapointed, but our centrist and reformist members are pleased. The bourgeois parties are cautiously optimistic about our apparent self-restraint.
go-to: civil_war_victory.scene.dry


@maintain
subtitle: Supported by: Reformists, Bourgeois Parties.
